      "slug": "self-couching",
      "term": "Self-couching",
      "definition": "A stitch technique where the same thread that crosses the shape is brought back to tie itself down, without a separate couching thread."
    }
  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Roumanian couching is a ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "self-couching",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "self-couching"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": " fill: the thread is carried across the shape, then the needle re-enters the fabric a short way from the exit point and comes up on the far side of the crossing thread. A short slanted tie stitch holds the laid thread down.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton 3 to 4 strands, or crewel wool"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fabric",
              "value": "Linen or crewel twill"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needle",
              "value": "Crewel needle size 7 or 8"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hoop",
              "value": "20 cm embroidery hoop"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Working a practice piece",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring the thread up at the left edge of the shape. Carry it across to the right edge and insert the needle just inside the right edge.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring the needle up a short distance inside the right edge, just below the crossing thread.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Take a short slanted stitch over the crossing thread toward the centre of the shape to tie it down.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Carry the thread across again for the next row, spacing it just below the previous tie stitch.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Common mistakes",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "intro": "Two common problems.",
          "items": [
            {
              "fix": "Mark parallel guide lines across the shape before starting. Equal spacing gives a regular pattern.",
              "cause": "The spacing between rows varies.",
              "symptom": "The laid threads are uneven"
            },
            {
              "fix": "The tie stitch should be short, about 3 to 4 mm, placed in the centre of the shape. Only the tie slant should show; the laid thread underneath should dominate.",
              "cause": "The tie stitch is too far from the edge.",
              "symptom": "The tie stitches are too long and dominate the design"
            }
          ],
